            "review_title": "Review at Cơm Tấm Múc",
            "review_text": "KiKi\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam26 contributions\n0\nDelicious and Clean Broken Rice at MUC\nAug 2024 • Friends\nThe broken rice with grilled pork belly was spot on. The pork belly was tender and juicy, with just the right amount of char and flavor. The balance between the fat and meat was perfect, tasty.\n\nThe mackerel was firm, not fishy at all, and the braised sauce was rich and savory with a nice tang from the tomatoes.\n\nHowever, the food did take a bit of time to prepare since the restaurant grills the meat fresh when you order. This is understandable given that the place is still new and doesn't have enough customers yet to keep the grill going constantly. My meal took about 15 minutes to arrive, but since the food was so delicious, the wait was totally worth it.\n\nThe place itself is cozy and clean, with a simple but welcoming vibe. The staff were friendly and quick, always with a smile.\n\nOverall, Múc is definitely a spot worth visiting. We all left feeling satisfied and happy, and we’ll definitely be back to try more dishes.\nRead more\nWritten August 15, 2024",
